{
    "background_story": "Gabriel was a brilliant geologist with a passion for rare minerals. His life's work was dedicated to studying the unique properties of olivenite, a copper arsenate mineral found in limited quantities around the world. Gabriel spent years researching and collecting samples, often venturing into remote areas to uncover new deposits. His groundbreaking research on olivenite's crystal structure and formation processes earned him international recognition and acclaim. As he delved deeper into his work, Gabriel became obsessed with finding the perfect specimen, one that would unlock the secrets of this enigmatic mineral. His quest took him to the depths of the earth, and though he faced countless challenges, Gabriel's relentless pursuit of knowledge was driven by an insatiable curiosity and love for the mysteries of the geological world.",
